# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences on what this project does and who it's for. -->

A FastAPI service in `backend/` and a React single-page app in `frontend/`, in one repository. The frontend calls the API through a client generated from the backend's OpenAPI document. [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) explains how the two connect.

## Quickstart

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [Bun](https://bun.sh), Node and make.

```bash
make install
make dev        # API on :8000, web on :4173
```

Open http://localhost:4173. The web dev server forwards `/api` to the API. To change a port or a setting for both parts, copy `.env.example` to `.env` and edit it; a variable exported in your shell still wins.

## Commands

Run from the repository root. Each target runs the matching command inside `backend/` and `frontend/`.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make dev` | Both dev servers |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check or fix lint and formatting |
| `make typecheck` | mypy and tsc |
| `make test` | Both parts' tests |
| `make api-client` | Regenerate the frontend's API client after a backend change |
| `make check` | Everything: each part's checks, the contract chain and a request through the proxy |

Run `make help` for the full list. Each part's own README covers its commands.

## Layout

```
backend/    FastAPI service: app/, tests/, its own Makefile and README
frontend/   React app on Vite: src/, tests/, e2e/, the generated client in src/api/generated/
docs/       ARCHITECTURE.md, how the parts connect
scripts/    check-pair.sh, the check that runs both parts together
```

